cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Hushline
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
version: 0.1.5
date-released: "2026-06-20"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/anulum/HushLine"
url: "https://anulum.github.io/HushLine/"
abstract: >-
  Hushline is a local command-output shaping utility. It runs a child command
  and filters, redacts, and bounds its stdout and stderr before the output
  reaches the caller, for deterministic, privacy-aware prompt chains and local
  automation. The same command contract is implemented by four independent
  cores in Go, Rust, Python, and Node.
authors:
